# The Dockerfile COPYs only the specific paths it needs (see its COPY
# instructions) — that explicit list, not this file, is what keeps
# secrets and native-platform cruft out of the image. Secrets arrive as
# build ARGs (see Dockerfile), not a copied file, so .env never needs
# to be in the build context at all.

android/
ios/
integration_test/
test/
tools/
fastlane/
docs/

build/
.dart_tool/
.fvm/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.hive

# .git IS part of the build context (not excluded) -- the build stage
# reads the current commit hash from it to stamp the build (see
# Dockerfile's GIT_COMMIT_SHA step / AppConst.gitCommitSha). It's only
# COPY'd into the intermediate build stage, never into the final nginx
# image that actually ships.
.github/
